      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T21:02:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this would be simpler with just an extra `eq` and an `or` instead of constructing two vectors and using `any`, e.g.:\n\n```suggestion\n            ResourceType resource_ty \u003d core::type::TypeToResourceType(type);\n            core::ir::Value* eq \u003d b.Equal(v, u32(resource_ty))-\u003eResult();\n\n            auto conv \u003d core::type::ConvertsFrom(type);\n            if (conv.has_value()) {\n                auto* cmp \u003d b.Equal(v, u32(conv.value()));\n                eq \u003d b.Or(eq, cmp)-\u003eResult();\n            }\n```\n\n(this also avoids the intermediate steps through uint32_t which avoids static_cast vs C-style casts, assuming it works with all compilers)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "507fd2b6f7df025b88258e9186c805d03c3d49ea",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
